t-6.1-sol | Assigned: 2026-10-17 15:00 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: continues the slice; commit 1 (R4) is merged to master as ce76c846; Architect ruled Part B and gave exact steps\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-pins (branch srvm-module-pins; HEAD 62121c7e = commit 1, ALREADY merged to origin/master ce76c846; tree clean). Read COMPLETELY ./collab/*architect-module-pins-review.report.md: Part B (ruling B.1 items 1-6: host modules DO participate; the lift records only used exports; two maps in `requires`: `:yin.k/modules {symbol -> manifest-address-string-or-nil}` and `:yin.k/host-exports {qualified-symbol -> profile-keyword}`; the lower's `check-modules!` with terminal `:module-pin-mismatch` / `:host-export-mismatch` and one collected `:yin.k/unsatisfied` with `:yin.k/discovery :complete` and `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {...} :yin.k/host-exports {...}}`, zero attaches) and Part C steps 8-16 and the threat model ./collab/*architect-fetch-threat-model.report.md sections 3, 4.2, 4.4, 4.5, 5, 7. EXECUTE steps 8-16 EXACTLY (lift collector in/near discharge!, encoder/decoder/validator + malformed-slot collection extending `:requires`, `check-modules!` replacing `check-install-admission!` (absorbing it: carried install children listed in `:yin.k/admitted-modules` fold into the same collected shape), driver seam forwarding `(:yin.k/admitted-modules (:config state))` from `driver/lowered` and the fenced recovery call plus one driver test with and without the config, tests T1-T5, T8-T10 as amended in the ruling, the five mutants of step 13, fixture re-mint with old -> new addresses in the report and a completed dated I-8 entry in docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md, the doc amendments of step 15 including closing the known-gaps rows (Q5, R4 landed, P2-1 driver seam closed) and fixing the stale Part-B statements Architect P3-2 listed (known-gaps Q5 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"blocked\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" row, continuation Q5 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"report specifies no carrier slot\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", UCF \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"blocked pending the host-export-profile slot/schema\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" text), tidy the lower-task docstring as P3-4). Also drop the trivially true assertion at rows_test ~:1396 (P3-5) and align the lift's strip with the lower's refusal predicate if trivial (P3-1: strip every keyword key in the yin.admit namespace). The fetch LOOP is NOT part of this slice (no fetch/clock/lease code in rows.cljc or the lower; T9 pins layering). RULES: no src/yang, no test/yang, no collab commits, never --yolo, no commit/stage; if any pinned A address, descriptor hash or golden OTHER than the rows fixtures carrying `requires` moves, STOP and report old/new; if the ruling is ambiguous (e.g. how an entry's `:address` is read for a module resolved through the family, what `requires` emits for empty maps), STOP that sub-part and report; never weaken an assertion. Verification foreground: per-iteration `clojure -M:test -e :slow` on the focused namespaces (rows-test, rows-custody-test, rows-checkpoint-test, remote-test, holder.*, safepoint-harness-test, frame-test, layout-test, stage-e-rows-test, linker-test, linker-manifest-test, mint-test) + `-r '^dao\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.jing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\..*'`; kondo on changed files (0 new); `git diff --check`; the whole JVM quick tier unrestricted at the end. No Node/Dart (orchestrator). Report ./collab/<ms>-engineer-module-pins-r2b.report.md with headers, per-step results, counts, fixtures old/new, mutants with named killers, what you STOPPED on, proposed commit split (code / tests+fixture / docs; driver seam separable?), truthful. End READY or BLOCKED.\\\\\\\\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-16 06:33:25 GMT\\\\\\\\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-16 13:33:25 +07\\\\\\\\nCoding-Agent: codex\\\\\\\\nSession-ID: unavailable (provider not exposed)\\\\\\\\nRole: VM Runtime\\\\\\\\nBranch: srvm-module-pins\\\\\\\\nBase: 62121c7e\\\\\\\\nBrief: collab/1793590000000-engineer-module-pins-r2b.prompt.md\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Module pins r2b: partial implementation, carrier stopped on ambiguity\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Mandatory stop\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe brief explicitly says to STOP the affected sub-part if the ruling is\\\\\\\\nambiguous, specifically including what `requires` emits for empty maps.\\\\\\\\nArchitect Part B.1.3 says \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Absent maps are not emitted when empty\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", but\\\\\\\\nimmediately mentions that empty trees are still emitted; step 8 says \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"empty\\\\\\\\nmaps handled as the existing requires keys handle empties\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". The existing lift\\\\\\\\nunconditionally emits empty trees, segments and cursor profiles. These produce\\\\\\\\ndifferent canonical bytes and fixture addresses. I did not choose between\\\\\\\\nomitting empty pin keys and always emitting both keys with `{}`. An asynchronous\\\\\\\\nclarification asks for exactly this choice; no answer received at report creation.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Per-step results\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n8. STOPPED the carrier collector/emission pending the empty-map decision.\\\\\\\\n   Independent P3-1 cleanup implemented: lift strips every top-level keyword\\\\\\\\n   key whose namespace is `yin.admit`, matching the lower's refusal predicate.\\\\\\\\n   Regression adds `:yin.admit/other` to the sender record and retains the\\\\\\\\n   decoded-row, refusal-before-attach, relift and installed-entry assertions.\\\\\\\\n9. Pending step 8: no new pin encoder/decoder/validator or malformed cases.\\\\\\\\n10. Pending carrier: existing install-admission gate remains; no claim of the\\\\\\\\n    new collected module/host-export refusal shape.\\\\\\\\n11. IMPLEMENTED: `bare-state` retains only the admitted-modules composition\\\\\\\\n    setting under `:config` (there was no `:config` field previously).\\\\\\\\n    `lowered` and the fenced-recovery call forward\\\\\\\\n    `(:yin.k/admitted-modules (:config state))`. `initial` documents the setting.\\\\\\\\n    `parked-installer-needs-composition-admission-test`