ngbuffer/capacity-key (or capacity\\\\\\\\n                                                   vm/default-stream-capacity)}))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn new-stream\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Create one ring buffer handle or throw.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  ([] (new-stream default-capacity))\\\\\\\\n  ([capacity]\\\\\\\\n   (let [result (make-stream capacity)]\\\\\\\\n     (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:140:          (fail (str \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Unable to resolve symbol: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" in this context\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n    (when-not (occurrence-origin? origin)\\\\\\\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Malformed source occurrence origin\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n                      {:rule :origin, :origin origin})))\\\\\\\\n    origin))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn loaded-code-floor\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The lowest entity id claimed by the segments in a `{segment-id image}`\\\\\\\\n   code map — each segment id minus its length — or 0 when none is loaded.\\\\\\\\n   A loader minting a fresh local segment id allocates below this floor\\\\\\\\n   (`semantic/load-ast` for projected AST batches, `semantic/load-vector`\\\\\\\\n   for canonical instruction vectors), so successive loads never collide\\\\\\\\n   with a live id.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  [code]\\\\\\\\n  (if (map? code)\\\\\\\\n    (reduce-kv (fn [floor seg image]\\\\\\\\n                 (if (and (integer? seg) (map? image))\\\\\\\\n                   (min floor (- seg (or (:length image) 0)))\\\\\\\\n                   floor))\\\\\\\\n               0\\\\\\\\n               code)\\\\\\\\n    0))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n;; Semantic bytecode: flat content-addressed rows\\\\\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n;; docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §2. One row `[id tag & slots]` per\\\\\\\\n;; distinct node; `id` is `(jing/segment-key [tag & slots])`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(def semantic-bytecode-grammar\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The Universal AST row-slot table (yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §2.3):\\\\\\\\n   tag -> ordered `[field kind]` slots, rather than executable bytecode. Position `i` of a\\\\\\\\n   row body (after the tag) holds the map field named at `i`, so this one\\\\\\\\n   table drives both projection and reconstruction.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  {:literal [[:value :data]],\\\\\\\\n   :variable [[:name :sym]],\\\\\\\\n   :lambda [[:params :syms] [:body :node]],\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:714:**2026-10-16, I-8 (module-pins slice, partial; R4 only).** Lower now\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:723:Part B.1.3 versus step 8. I-8 is not complete.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:10:> S7.11 lists the acceptance blockers that keep this warning standing until\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:36:(S7.6.1); S7.11 records the remaining definition-frame obligations.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:41:(7.2.1, 7.4.3, 7.7.8, 7.9, 7.11.1). The amendment is published design:\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:66:and 7.6.1a (the source association and its completeness rule); 7.11 and\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:67:7.11.1 require the frame validator and cross-engine canonical equality\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:86:Every sentence in §7.2–§7.9 is a rule of the proposed protocol. §7.11 records\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:556:transition; see the revision log in S7.11. The de Bruijn images carry\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:598:`:yin.k/missing :yin.k/trees` and discovery is `:incomplete` (§7.6.5),\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:625:miss is `:yin.k/unsatisfied` n