odule-pins commit 2 | P1 |\\\\\\\\n| Composition fetch loop per-run lease and budget absent | fetch threat model §4.3; reserved `:lease` policy | composition | outside module-pins slice; no fetch loop added | P2 |\\\\\\\\n| Holder driver passes no admitted-modules map; install-child handoff through the driver refuses | Architect module-pins review P2-1 | VM Runtime | implemented in module-pins r2b (uncommitted): composition config retained and forwarded to lowering and fenced recovery; parked-installer driver regression covers absent and admitted config | P2 |\\\\\\\\n  contract; the receiver-side pin check remains required.\\\\\\\\n- **Q6, conservatism of the live-code rule.** `live-pcs` follows both\\\\\\\\n  successor edges of every branch and enters every reachable closure\\\\\\\\n  body, with no constant propagation. The harness's `(if false (fn []\\\\\\\\n  ghost) (next-of c))` case transports only because the lift happens at\\\\\\\\n  a safepoint **after** the branch (the resume pc is past it, so the\\\\\\\\n  dead arm is unreachable by edges); the same program lifted at a\\\\\\\\n  safepoint **before** the branch would refuse `ghost` although the arm\\\\\\\\n  can never run. Is \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"reachable by control-flow edges, never by value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  the intended precision, accepting the false refusals it implies for\\\\\\\\n  constant-dead code?\\\\\\\\n- **Q7, host-class primitives behind a shadow.** `:host-state-primitive`\\\\\\\\n  refuses only when the name reaches the primitive step of the answering\\\\\\\\n  order; the same name bound in `E` or the active store lifts (codex\\\\\\\\n  round 2 confirmed). Intended, or should a host-class primitive name\\\\\\\\n  refuse regardless of shadowing?\\\\\\\\n- **Q8, preflight attachment cost.** `attaches?` validates and analyses\\\\\\\\n  every carried vector (and every install image) by attaching it into a\\\\\\\\n  throwaway receiver, and restore attaches it again. Codex found it pure\\\\\\\\n  and only duplicated CPU. Accept, or ask the kernel for a validate-only\\\\\\\\n  entry point?\\\\\\\\n- **Q9, Law 2 outside a fresh receiver.** The id counter is adopted as\\\\\\\\n  `max(local, carried)`; a receiver whose construction mints more ids\\\\\\\\n  than the carrier relifts to a different root (draft §9 already scopes\\\\\\\\n  the law to the fresh-receiver context). No harness case has a\\\\\\\\n  non-fresh receiver. Add one as a documented non-law, or leave it?\\\\\\\\n- **Q10, the `:running` wire phase's future.** If Q1 narrows the phase\\\\\\\\n  set, row 11 disappears from the matrix and the `:install` row's phase\\\\\\\\n  slot becomes a constant; if not, row 11 stays a synthetic case. Which?\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Revision 5 (after 6c) adds the three questions the rulings left\\\\\\\\n(`collab/1792360000000-architect-6c-rulings.report.md`); they are\\\\\\\\nnumbered on their own, as 6c Q1-Q3, so the 6b numbering above stands.**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **6c Q1, the native-lane matrix scope (changes acceptance counts).\\\\\\\\n  ACCEPTED by the owner on 2026-10-13.** The de Bruijn lanes run the\\\\\\\\n  shared fragment: law 4 on 61 of the 89 cases, law 5 on 350 of the 534\\\\\\\\n  transfers, tail acceptance on rows 6 and 20 only.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **Authority grounding and wiring.** The arbitration `dao.space`, its\\\\\\\\n  transactor as grantor, the occurrence ledger with epochs, and the\\\\\\\\n  attribution resolver `dao.lease.md` requires, are composition duties; the\\\\\\\\n  first composition to ship UCF is `yin.repl.core`'s handoff demo, and\\\\\\\\n  its wiring becomes the worked example. A composition without a\\\\\\\\n  transactable space offers `:yin.k/fork` only.\\\\\\\\n- **Receiver module satisfaction and install admission (2026-10-16).**\\\\\\\\n  Architect verdict C requires registry bindings pinned by manifest address\\\\\\\\n  (§7.6.4/§7.6.5) and receiver re-discharge before attachment. The module-pin\\\\\\\\n  carrier uses `:yin.k/host-exports` in `requires` for used host export profile\\\\\\\\n  addresses (Architect Part B, ruled 2026-10-16). Implementation is pending:\\\\\\\\n  r2b stopped on conflicting empty-map emission instructions. Name presence\\\\\\\\n  does not establish equal-address satisfaction.\\\\\\\\n  Carried install admission (R4) is implemented by the lower's explicit\\\\\\\\n  `:yin.k/admitted-modules {name manifest-address}` option, default empty, and\\\\\\\\n  the lift never carries sender admission evidence; a carried admission field\\\\\\\\n  is refused as `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response`. The fetch loop remains\\\\\\\\n  composition work: fetch before the grant proposal (14.2.3 step 2), retry\\\\\\\\n  the same pack bytes, at most one require per missing module and two\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nTesting yin.vm.linker.layering-test\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRan 33 tests containing 173 assertions.\\\\\\\\n0 failures, 0 errors.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ncollab/1793600000000-engineer-module-pins-r2c.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:73:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_36\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '430,458p' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md; sed -n '2774,2790p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; git diff -- test/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc test/yin/vm/linker/layering_test.clj\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"[T :task\\\\\\\\n   version          ; 3                       (gated first, §8)\\\\\\\\n   contract         ; {:yin.code/contract \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"v4\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :yin.k/version 1}, the one profile map (§2)\\\\\\\\n   kind             ; :blocked | :parked | :halted\\\\\\\\n   role             ; :root | :child\\\\\\\\n   id-counter       ; N                       (UCF §7.6.3)\\\\\\\\n   free-env-