 install admission (R4) is implemented by the lower's explicit\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2873:  `:yin.k/admitted {name manifest-address}` option, default empty, and\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2874:  sender admission evidence is dropped on restore. The fetch loop remains\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:3190:- Invariant: One occurrence has at most one admitted holder, and each\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:3319:   names a carried record. Both wire phases running/parked are admitted,\\\\\\\\nAGENTS.md\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ncollab/1793560000000-engineer-module-pins-r2a.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:18:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_7\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '1630,1660p;1830,1875p;2224,2246p;2273,2298p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '1,65p;1367,1425p' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc; sed -n '1,65p;395,515p' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc; cat collab/1793530000000-engineer-module-pins.prompt.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(declare lift-task*)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- install-node\\\\\\\\n  [ctx mn inst opts]\\\\\\\\n  (let [{:keys [phase parent response]} inst]\\\\\\\\n    (when-not (contains? #{:running :parked} phase)\\\\\\\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/phase phase}))\\\\\\\\n    (when-not (try (cbor/encode response) true\\\\\\\\n                   (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _e false))\\\\\\\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :install-response {:yin.k/name mn}))\\\\\\\\n    (node :install [mn phase parent response\\\\\\\\n                    (lift-task* (:vm inst) (:serve! ctx)\\\\\\\\n                                (assoc (dissoc opts :free-env) :path (conj (:path ctx) mn)) :child)])))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- lift-task*\\\\\\\\n  [m serve! opts role]\\\\\\\\n  (when (seq (:ready-queue m))\\\\\\\\n    (outcome! :yin.k/not-quiescent nil {:yin.k/ready (count (:ready-queue m))}))\\\\\\\\n  (when-some [h (unliftable-hold m)]\\\\\\\\n    (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :reason-mismatch {:yin.k/hold h}))\\\\\\\\n  (when (some? (:control m))\\\\\\\\n    (outcome! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc (get-in m [:control :pc])}))\\\\\\\\n  (let [value (:value m)\\\\\\\\n        active? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? (:parked m) (:id value)))\\\\\\\\n        kind (cond active? :parked\\\\\\\\n                   (seq (:wait-set m)) :blocked\\\\\\\\n                   (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? m) :halted\\\\\\\\n(defn- check-install!\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"One install record: a phase the engine holds a carried child in, the\\\\\\\\n   retained response link-install reads (status, manifest naming this\\\\\\\\n   module, exports) with the image spawn-child loads, the response's link\\\\\\\\n   id equal to the row's parent (the engine settles only the response of\\\\\\\\n   its own link), the image the manifest names (continuation §11 Q3: the\\\\\\\\n   manifest's :yin.semantic/code derivation record is the response's\\\\\\\\n   :derivation, from the manifest's tree to the image's A), and a child\\\\\\\\n   that is blocked: the engine links a halted child in the sweep it\\\\\\\\n   halts in.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  [recv inst]\\\\\\\\n  (let [[mn phase parent response child] (:slots inst)\\\\\\\\n        manifest (when (map? response) (:manifest response))\\\\\\\\n        child-kind (nth (:slots child) 2)]\\\\\\\\n    (when-not (contains? #{:running :parked} phase)\\\\\\\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-phase {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/phase phase}))\\\\\\\\n    (when-not (and (map? response) (= :ok (:status response)) (map? manifest)\\\\\\\\n                   (= mn (:yin.module/name manifest))\\\\\\\\n                   (coll? (:yin.module/exports manifest)) (every? symbol? (:yin.module/exports manifest))\\\\\\\\n                   (map? (:image response)) (attaches? recv (:value (:image response)) nil))\\\\\\\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-response {:yin.k/name mn}))\\\\\\\\n    (when-not (and (some? parent) (= parent (:yin.link/id response)))\\\\\\\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-link-id {:yin.k/name mn}))\\\\\\\\n    (let [record (:derivation response)]\\\\\\\\n      (when-not (and (map? record)\\\\\\\\n                     (jing/segment-matches? (get-in manifest [:yin.module/derivations :yin.semantic/code]) record)\\\\\\\\n                     (= (:yin.ledger/input record) (:yin.module/tree manifest))\\\\\\\\n                     (jing/segment-matches? (:yin.ledger/output record) (:value (:image response))))\\\\\\\\n        (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-image {:yin.k/name mn})))\\\\\\\\n    (when-not (= :blocked child-kind)\\\\\\\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-child {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/task-kind child-kind}))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- check-pendings!\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Step 8, pending and operations: role, kind, parked id, every :install\\\\\\\\n   pending names a carried install, every install record.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  [recv task role]\\\\\\\\n  (let [[_ _ kind role' _ _ _ _ parked _ _ _ installs waits parked-id] (:slots task)]\\\\\\\\n    (when-not (= role role') (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :role {:yin.k/role role'}))\\\\\\\\n    (let [names (into #{} (map #(first (:slots %))) installs)]\\\\\\\\n      (doseq [w waits]\\\\\\\\n        (let [[reason n] (:slots (second (:slots w)))]\\\\\\\\n          (when (and (= :install reason) (not (contains? names n)))\\\\\\\\n            (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name n})))))\\\\\\\\n    (case kind\\\\\\\\n      :halted (when (seq waits) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\\\\\\\\n                                     [mid (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (value v)])) (partition 2 (:slots s)))])))\\\\\\\\n                         module-stores)\\\\\\\\n            parked' (into {} (map (fn [[p _]] [p (parked-record p)])) parked-index)\\\\\\\\n            entries (mapv entry waits)\\\\\\\\n            link (some #(let [[reason _ _ req resp] (:slots (second (:slots %)))]\\\\\\\\n                          (when (contains? #{:link-request :link-response} reason) [req resp]))\\\\\\\\n                       waits)\\\\\\\\n            [base installs'] (reduce (fn [[r acc] inst]\\\\\\\\n                                       (let [[mn phase parent response child] (:slots inst)\\\\\\\\n                                             ;; Only the receiver's admitted name/address permits\\\\\\\\n                                             ;; this child. Drop the sender's decision before\\\\\\\\n                                             ;; link-install can publish it as local evidence.\\\\\\\\n                                             response (dissoc response :yin.admit/id :yin.admit/decision\\\\\\\\n                                                              :yin.admit/asserters :yin.admit/address)\\\\\\\\n                                             [spawned r'] (spawn-child r response mn (:fenced? custody))]\\\\\\\\n                                         [r' (assoc acc mn {:phase phase :parent parent :response response\\\\\\\\n                                                            :vm (restore-task spawned child handles custody false)})]))\\\\\\\\n                                     [base {}] installs)\\\\\\\\n            fe (keyed free-env)\\\\\\\\n            resources (merge (:resources base)\\\\\\\\n                             (into {} (map (fn [[identity k]] [k (get handles identity)])) stream-keys)\\\\\\\\n                             (into {} (map (fn [[c body]]\\\\\\\\n                                             [(get cell-keys c) {:stream-id (stream-key (first (:slots body)))\\\\\\\\n(defn lower-task\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic machine of the\\\\\\\\n   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\\\\\\\\n   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\\\\\\\\n   primitives), each step over the whole tree before the next, then\\\\\\\\n   custody (check-custody!), all before the first attach! (step 11); then\\\\\\\\n   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the\\\\\\\\n   restored machine, or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\\\\\\\\n   opts: :budget; :yin.k/admitted, a composition-supplied {name manifest-address}\\\\\\\\n   for carried install children (default empty, fail closed; carried admission\\\\\\\\n   evidence is dropped); :exclusive, refuse a fork root; :grant and :protection,\\\\\\\\n   required by a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's reader\\\\\\\\n   contract: the grant names :checkpoint, the pack address, its lease,\\\\\\\\n   holder, tenure and evidence; :protection maps every stream identity of\\\\\\\\n   the tree to its class); :fenced, an administrative rehydration that\\\\\\\\n   skips the grant and restores every task of the tree gated :exporting,\\\\\\\\n   its waits in :yin.k/recovery-waits and its parked records in\\\\\\\\n   :yin.k/recovery-parked (none in the scheduler), its id counter the\\\\\\\\n   carried one exactly and :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids mapping each cursor\\\\\\\\n   cell's resource key to its carried cell id.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))\\\\\\\\n  ([recv wire attach! opts]\\\\\\\\n   (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]\\\\\\\\n     (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))\\\\\\\\n     ;; each step over the whole tree before the next (§3.3)\\\\\\\\n     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies!]\\\\\\\\n(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows-test\\\\\\\\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\\\\\\\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\\\\\\\\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\\\\\\\\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\\\\\\\\n            [dao.jing.cbor-fixtures :as fx]\\\\\\\\n            [yang.python.antlr.int-contract-fixtures :as ints]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as support]\\\\\\\\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.frame-test :as ft]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.malformed-rows :as malformed]))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn error\\\\\\\\n  [f]\\\\\\\\n  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn task-node\\\\\\\\n  [cursor-cells result]\\\\\\\\n  (rows/node :task [3 rows/profile :halted :root 0 (rows/node :bindings [])\\\\\\\\n                    (rows/node :store []) [] (rows/node :parked-table [])\\\\\\\\n                    (rows/node :cursor-cells (mapcat identity cursor-cells)) {} {} [] [] nil result nil]))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn cursor-cell-body\\\\\\\\n  [stream position]\\\\\\\\n  (rows/node :cursor-cell-body [(rows/node :stream [stream {:peer stream}]) position]))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn fixture\\\\\\\\n  [a b x y]\\\\\\\\n  (let [payload [:row (rows/node :map\\\\\\\\n                                 [[:lit 'both] [:row (rows/node :set [[:cursor-cell x] [:cursor-cell y]])]\\\\\\\\n                                  [:lit 'one] [:cursor-cell x]\\\\\\\\n                                  [:lit 'streams] [:row (rows/node :set [[:row (rows/node :stream [a {:peer a}])]\\\\\\\\n                                                                         [:row (rows/node :stream [b {:peer b}])]])]\\\\\\\\n                                  [:lit 'cursors] [:row (rows/node :map [[:cursor-cell x] [:lit :x] [:cursor-cell y] [:lit :y]])]])]\\\\\\\\n        task (task-node [[x (cursor-cell-body a 0)] [y (cursor-cell-body b 0)]] [:lit nil])]\\\\\\\\n    (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots task) 6 (rows/node :store ['payload payload])))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(declare portable-frame)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- encoded\\\\\\\\n  [x]\\\\\\\\n  (cond (and (map? x) (contains? x :yin.k/row)) [:row (:yin.k/row x)]\\\\\\\\n        (and (map? x) (contains? x :yin.k/cursor-cell)) [:cursor-cell (:yin.k/cursor-cell x)]\\\\\\\\n        :else [:lit x]))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- portable-value\\\\\\\\n  [m x]\\\\\\\\n  ;; Classify native test values into the decoded codec domain. No seals\\\\\\\\n  ;; travel. Captures retain their entire act and K; closures retain the\\\\\\\\n  ;; code address, binders, lexical bindings and module context.\\\\\\\\n  (cond\\\\\\\\n    (values/continuation? x)\\\\\\\\n    {:yin.k/row (rows/node :reified\\\\\\\\n     :cljd (println \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"SKIP host-collapse: slash-crossed identifiers remain distinct on Dart\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(deftest carried-install-requires-receiver-admission\\\\\\\\n  (let [sender-record {:yin.admit/id \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sender-only\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n                       :yin.admit/decision :allow\\\\\\\\n                       :yin.admit/asserters #{'sender}\\\\\\\\n                       :yin.admit/address :sender-only}\\\\\\\\n        source (update-in (support/parked-installer)\\\\\\\\n                          [:installs 'host.mod :response] merge sender-record)\\\\\\\\n        wire (support/lift source nil)\\\\\\\\n        address (jing/segment-key (:manifest (support/module-response)))\\\\\\\\n        recv (support/new-machine)]\\\\\\\\n    (doseq [opts [{} {:yin.k/admitted {'other.mod address}}\\\\\\\\n                  {:yin.k/admitted {'host.mod :wrong-address}}\\\\\\\\n                  {:yin.k/admitted {'host.mod nil}}]]\\\\\\\\n      (let [{:keys [attach! count]} (support/attacher)\\\\\\\\n            refusal (error #(rows/lower-task recv wire attach! opts))]\\\\\\\\n        (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status refusal)))\\\\\\\\n        (is (= {:yin.k/modules {'host.mod address}} (:yin.k/missing refusal)))\\\\\\\\n        (is (zero? @count))\\\\\\\\n        (is (empty? (:installs recv)))))\\\\\\\\n    (let [{:keys [attach! count]} (support/attacher)\\\\\\\\n          restored (rows/lower-task (assoc recv :attach-stream attach!) wire attach! {:yin.k/admitted {'host.mod address}})\\\\\\\\n          response (get-in restored [:installs 'host.mod :response])\\\\\\\\n          child (get-in restored [:installs 'host.mod :vm])\\\\\\\\n          wait (first (:wait-set child))]\\\\\\\\n      (is (pos? @count))\\\\\\\\n      (is (not-any? #(contains? response %) (keys sender-record)))\\\\\\\\n      (stream/append! (get (:resources child) (:stream-id wait)) :resume)\\\\\\\\n      (let [done (vm/run restored)\\\\\\\\n            installed (module/module-entry (:modules (:modules done)) 'host.mod)]\\\\\\\\n        (is (= 42 (:value done)))\\\\\\\\n        (is (= address (:address installed)))\\\\\\\\n        (is (not (contains? installed :admission)))))))\\\\\\\\n(ns yin.vm.ucf.holder.export-test\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"D8 over the row carrier (UCF 7.7.4; r3 1.8 and 1.9; phase 7b): the\\\\\\\\n   exporting state, the prepare/encode split over rows/lift-task, the\\\\\\\\n   export-recovery object version 2, its fenced rehydration and the abort\\\\\\\\n   rule. Every machine is a semantic machine the real engine\\\\\\\\n   parked (yin.vm.ucf.rows-support); counting handles show what the gate,\\\\\\\\n   the encode and the rehydration touch.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\\\\\\\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\\\\\\\\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\\\\\\\\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\\\\\\\\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.export :as export]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\\\\\\\\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as rs]))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n;; Machines, the exporter, the receiver's attach\\\\\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- throws?\\\\\\\\n  [thunk]\\\\\\\\n  (try (thunk) false\\\\\\\\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ true)))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- ring\\\\\\\\n  [capacity]\\\\\\\\n  (:dao.stream/handle\\\\\\\\n    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\\\\\\\\n                         ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity})))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- index\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The composition's source index, as the composition reads it.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  []\\\\\\\\n  @rs/source-index)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- two-streams\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Parks on a read of the first stream; the store also holds the second\\\\\\\\n   stream and a cursor on each, so the lift reaches two streams.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  []\\\\\\\\n  (rs/let1 'a {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\\\\\\\\n           (rs/let1 'b {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\\\\\\\\n                    (rs/then (rs/def! 'held-a (rs/cursor-of (rs/v 'a)))\\\\\\\\n                             (rs/then (rs/def! 'held-b (rs/cursor-of (rs/v 'b)))\\\\\\\\n                                      (rs/next-of (rs/v 'held-a)))))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- parked-machine\\\\\\\\n  []\\\\\\\\n  (vm/run (rs/load-ast (rs/new-machine) (two-streams))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- served-table\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A `serve!` that counts its calls and answers one stable identity per\\\\\\\\n   handle.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  []\\\\\\\\n                 (compare-and-set! first-handle nil h)\\\\\\\\n                 (when (= h @first-handle) served-answer))\\\\\\\\n        refused (export/prepare m' record stingy nil (index))]\\\\\\\\n    (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status refused)) (pr-str refused))\\\\\\\\n    (is (= 1 (count (get-in refused [:record :served]))))\\\\\\\\n    (testing \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a retry with the returned record never re-serves that stream\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      (let [asked (atom [])\\\\\\\\n            {:keys [serve!]} (served-table)\\\\\\\\n            retry (export/prepare m' (:record refused)\\\\\\\\n                                  (fn [h]\\\\\\\\n                                    (swap! asked conj h)\\\\\\\\n                                    (serve! h))\\\\\\\\n                                  nil (index))]\\\\\\\\n        (is (= :ok (:status retry)) (pr-str retry))\\\\\\\\n        (is (not-any? #(= @first-handle %) @asked))\\\\\\\\n        (is (= 1 (count @asked)) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"only the other stream\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(deftest a-custody-refusal-after-the-walk-keeps-what-the-walk-served-test\\\\\\\\n  ;; phase-7a D4: the row lift serves while it walks and decides the\\\\\\\\n  ;; protection and exhaustion refusals after; the record accounts for it\\\\\\\\n  (doseq [[label header expected]\\\\\\\\n          [[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"an enrolled write without an operation id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n            (rs/header 0 rs/origin #{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}) :unprotected-pending]\\\\\\\\n           [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"an exhausted counter\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n            (rs/header rows/max-exact rs/origin #{}) :op-seq-exhausted]]]\\\\\\\\n    (testing label\\\\\\\\n      (let [{m :machine record :record} (export/enter (rs/parked-writer))\\\\\\\\n            {:keys [calls serve!]} (served-table)\\\\\\\\n            refused (export/prepare m record serve! header (index))\\\\\\\\n            served @calls]\\\\\\\\n        (is (= :yin.k/non-portable (:yin.k/status refused)) (pr-str refused))\\\\\\\\n        (is (= expected (:yin.k/kind refused)))\\\\\\\\n        (is (pos? served) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"the walk served before the refusal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n        (is (= served (count (get-in refused [:record :served]))) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"and the record retains every answer\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n        (export/prepare m (:record refused) serve! header (index))\\\\\\\\n        (is (= served @calls) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a retry serves nothing twice\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n;; Freeze: recovery version 2\\\\\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(deftest the-recovery-object-is-the-pack-and-holder-local-state-test\\\\\\\\n  (let [{:keys [frozen prepared machine]} (frozen-of (rs/parked-explicit))\\\\\\\\n        recovery (cbor/decode (:bytes frozen))\\\\\\\\n        published (export/encode machine (:record prepared))]\\\\\\\\n    (is (= :ok (:status frozen)) (pr-str frozen))\\\\\\\\n    (is (= #{:yin.k/export-recovery :yin.k/version :yin.k/pack-address :yin.k/root\\\\\\\\n             :yin.k/pack-bytes :yin.k/header :yin.k/state}\\\\\\\\n           (set (keys recovery)))\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"one body: no snapshot, no descriptors (the pack carries them)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n    (is (= 2 (:yin.k/version recovery)))\\\\\\\\n    (is (= (:address published) (:pack-address frozen) (:yin.k/pack-address recovery)))\\\\\\\\n    (is (= (:root published) (:root frozen) (:yin.k/root recovery)))\\\\\\\\n    (is (= (vec (:bytes published)) (vec (:pack-bytes frozen))\\\\\\\\n           (vec (jing/base64->bytes (:yin.k/pack-bytes recovery)))))\\\\\\\\n    (is (jing/segment-bytes-match? (:address frozen) (:bytes frozen)))\\\\\\\\n    (is (= #{:gate :origins :issues :issued :children} (set (keys (:yin.k/state recovery)))))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n;; Rehydrate: fenced, reproducible, without program IO\\\\\\\\n;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(deftest complete-export-recovery-is-fenced-and-reproducible-test\\\\\\\\n  (doseq [[label source header] [[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a parked reader\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (rs/parked-reader) nil]\\\\\\\\n                                 [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"an explicit park\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (rs/parked-explicit) nil]\\\\\\\\n                                 [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"an installer\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (rs/parked-installer) nil]\\\\\\\\n                                 [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a parked reader under a header\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (rs/parked-reader) (rs/header 0 nil #{})]\\\\\\\\n                                 [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a halted root under a header\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (rs/halted-machine) (rs/header 0 rs/origin #{})]]]\\\\\\\\n    (testing label\\\\\\\\n      (let [{:keys [frozen record prepared]} (frozen-of source header)\\\\\\\\n            {:keys [attaches calls attach]} (counting-attach)\\\\\\\\n            restored (rehydrate frozen (rs/new-machine) attach)]\\\\\\\\n        (is (= :ok (:status frozen)) (pr-str frozen))\\\\\\\\n        (is (= :ok (:status restored)) (pr-str restored))\\\\\\\\n        (is (= :exporting (vm/gate-mode (:machine restored))))\\\\\\\\n        (is (empty? (:wait-set (:machine restored))))\\\\\\\\n        (is (empty? (:parked (:machine restored))))\\\\\\\\n        (is (= (count (:wait-set record)) (count (get-in restored [:record :wait-set]))))\\\\\\\\n        (is (= (set (keys (:parked record))) (set (keys (get-in restored [:record :parked])))))\\\\\\\\n        (is (nil? (get-in restored [:machine :yin.k/custody])) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"no custody is restored\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n        (is (zero? @calls) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"no read, write, mint or close\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n        (is (= (count (into #{} (map :dao.stream/identity) (vals (get-in prepared [:record :served]))))\\\\\\\\n               @attaches)\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"every stream attached, once\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n        (is (reproduces? frozen restored) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"the published pack, byte for byte\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(deftest recovery-requires-receiver-install-admission-test\\\\\\\\n  (let [{:keys [frozen]} (frozen-of (rs/parked-installer))\\\\\\\\n        address (jing/segment-key (:manifest (rs/module-response)))]\\\\\\\\n    (doseq [admitted [nil {'host.mod :wrong-address}]]\\\\\\\\n      (let [{:keys [attaches attach]} (counting-attach)\\\\\\\\n            refused (export/rehydrate-fenced\\\\\\\\n                      (rs/new-machine) (:bytes frozen)\\\\\\\\n                      {:address (:address frozen) :attach attach\\\\\\\\n                       :yin.k/admitted admitted})]\\\\\\\\n        (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status refused)))\\\\\\\\n        (is (= {:yin.k/modules {'host.mod address}} (:yin.k/missing refused)))\\\\\\\\n        (is (zero? @attaches))))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(deftest a-restarted-abort-is-refused-test\\\\\\\\n  (let [{:keys [frozen]} (frozen-of (rs/parked-reader))\\\\\\\\n        restored (rehydrate frozen)]\\\\\\\\n    (is (= :ok (:status restored)) (pr-str restored))\\\\\\\\n    (is (true? (get-in restored [:record :recovered?])))\\\\\\\\n    (is (= [:yin.k/refused :restarted]\\\\\\\\n           ((juxt :yin.k/status :yin.k/reason)\\\\\\\\n            (export/abort (:machine restored) (:record restored) [] nil))))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(deftest recovery-restores-fresh-name-state-without-receiver-contamination-test\\\\\\\\n  (let [source (assoc (rs/parked-reader) :origins 42 :id-counter 88 :yin.k/issued 77)\\\\\\\\n        {:keys [frozen]} (frozen-of source)\\\\\\\\n        restored (rehydrate frozen\\\\\\\\n                            (assoc (rs/new-machine) :origins 99 :id-counter 100\\\\\\\\n                                   :store {'receiver-local :wrong} :yin.k/issued 33\\\\\\\\n                                   :yin.k/closes [{:receiver-local true}])\\\\\\\\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-17 04:00:00 GMT\\\\\\\\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-17 11:00:00 +07\\\\\\\\nCoding-Agent: codex\\\\\\\\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\\\\\\\\n# Task: module-identity pins on the row carrier + receiver-side re-check + carried install children admitted by the receiver (Architect threat model verdict \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"C\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" + R4), uncommitted\\\\\\\\nRole: VM Runtime\\\\\\\\nImplementers:\\\\\\\\n- Model: gpt-6.1-sol | Assigned: 2026-10-17 11:00 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: owner said \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dispatch it to codex\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; Architect (Fable) reviews before any commit; this is a security-relevant format change\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-pins (branch srvm-module-pins @ origin/master). Read COMPLETELY: ./collab/*architect-fetch-threat-model.report.md (the Architect's threat model; sections 3 (routes R1-R13), 4.1-4.5, 5, 6 verdict, 7 tests and docs) and ./collab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md row on Q5. IMPLEMENT the verdict: (1) CARRIER: the task row's `requires` carries `:yin.k/modules {module-name manifest-address-or-nil}` (UCF section 7.6.4 form): the lift keeps the registry entry's `:address` for every registry-answered namespaced free name that discharge! answers via the registry (rows.cljc ~:1615-1617; a host-registered module has no address: nil, satisfied only by a host module of that name with equal export profiles via module/host-export-profile). Update the row grammar tables (docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md section 5.x, UCF 7.6.4/7.6.5 pointers), the row encoder/decoder and validators, restore. Packs re-mint: regenerate test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/rows-checkpoint-v3.txt via the existing rows-checkpoint-fixtures/render route (see how 9ab9e792 did it) and record a dated entry in docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md (I-8); no backward compatibility is owed. (2) LOWER re-check (B): `check-dependencies!` (rows.cljc ~:1898) re-discharges registry-answered names against the RECEIVER's registry by EQUAL ADDRESS (not name presence): a missing or different module refuses BEFORE attach with the exact outcome of section 4.2 (`:yin.k/unsatisfied`, `:yin.k/discovery :complete`, `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {...} :obligations #{...}}`), kind `:module-pin-mismatch` naming both addresses when the receiver holds a different address (words of engine.cljc:1388-1393 `:dependency-pin-mismatch`). The lower stays pure over the receiver value and attaches nothing on refusal (attach-count law); the receiver's registry is still kept as given. (3) R4: carried `:install` children: the lower refuses a child unless its manifest address is in a composition-supplied opts set `{:yin.k/admitted {name address}}` (default empty = fail closed), as `:yin.k/unsatisfied {:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}` before any attach (section 4.4); and at `link-install` (engine.cljc ~:1436-1443) the copied sender `:admission` record must not stand for the receiver's decision: replace it by the receiver's (opts-supplied) record or drop it, as the report specifies. (4) Documentation: continuation 2.5 and 7.2 (the lower now re-discharges registry names by pinned address; Q5 answered C), UCF 7.11, the refusal shape, and the FORBIDDEN list for a composition's fetch loop (section 4.2 last bullet, section 5) in the right design doc; update docs/agents/known-gaps.md rows (Q5, R4 install-child admission). The fetch LOOP itself is NOT part of this slice (composition policy; no fetch code in the VM or lower; do not add one). TESTS (portable .cljc, section 7.1): pin equal-address satisfaction, different-address refusal naming both addresses, missing-module refusal before attach with attach-count zero, host-module nil pin with equal and unequal profiles, install child refused with empty admitted set and accepted when listed, `link-install` no longer copies the sender's admission, the decoded pack round-trips the new slot, malformed slot refused (add to malformed_rows UCF collection like the :equality-collapse entry), and a mutant for each (name-only satisfaction regress: test fails). RULES: no src/yang, no test/yang, no collab commits, no `--yolo`; if any pinned A address, descriptor hash or golden other than rows fixtures carrying requires/install moves, STOP and report old/new; if the spec in the report is ambiguous or you need a decision (e.g. where the host-module profile is recorded), STOP that sub-part and report; never weaken an assertion; no commit/stage. Foreground lanes: kondo on changed files (0 new); focused `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-custody-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-checkpoint-test -n yin.vm.ucf.remote-test -n yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test -n yin.vm.semantic.frame-test -n yin.vm.linker-test -n yin.vm.linker-manifest-test -n yin.vm.mint-test -n yin.vm.semantic.layout-test` and `-r '^dao\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.jing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\..*'`; then the whole JVM quick tier `clojure -M:test -e :slow` (unrestricted; `bb gen:python-antlr` first if the lexer is missing). No Node/Dart (orchestrator). Report ./collab/<ms>-engineer-module-pins.report.md with Completed-GMT/Completed-Local/Coding-Agent/Session-ID: per-part what changed, fixtures moved (old/new addresses), counts, mutants, what you STOPPED on, file-to-commit mapping (code / tests / docs), truthful. End READY or BLOCKED.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ncollab/1793560000000-engineer-module-pins-r2a.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:21:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_9\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg -n 'canonical-under|defn lift|defn lower|rows/encode|update-in.*slots.*12' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_support.cljc; sed -n '1810,1830p;2755,2767p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '413,426p' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md; sed -n '2330,2342p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md; sed -n '714,730p' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md; rg -n 'defn.*reproduces|defn.*rehydrate|defn.*frozen-of' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc; rg -n ':yin.k/admitted' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/{holder/ledger,holder/driver}.cljc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_support.cljc:359:(defn lift-opts\\\\\\\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_support.cljc:366:(defn lift\\\\\\\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:178:(deftest canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant\\\\\\\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:181:        ca (rows/canonical-under a {:lane-a/s1 :s1 :lane-a/s2 :s2})\\\\\\\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:182:        cb (rows/canonical-under b {:lane-b/s2 :s1 :lane-b/s1 :s2})]\\\\\\\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:185:           (:yin.k/root (rows/canonical-under\\\\\\\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:191:           (:yin.k/kind (error #(rows/canonical-under a {:lane-a/s1 :s1})))))))\\\\\\\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:300:    (is (= (:yin.k/root (rows/canonical-under wire {:child/s :child :root/s :root}))\\\\\\\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:301:           (:yin.k/root (rows/emit (rows/decode (rows/canonical-under wire {:child/s :child :root/s :root}))))))))\\\\\\\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:355:    (is (= (:yin.k/root (rows/canonical-under (rows/emit a) ident))\\\\\\\\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:356:           (:yin.k/root (rows/canonical-under (rows/emit b) ident))))))\\\\\\\\n| custody | `check-custody!` | `custody-baseline` over the tree; fork refused under `:exclusive`; halted exclusive needs no grant; blocked/parked exclusive validates grant evidence, pack checkpoint, binding, lease/holder, arbitration, epoch, live tenure and input prefix, then protection in both directions and op-id presence against enrollment; `:fenced` skips grant/protection | grammar's `:yin.k/undecodable` kinds; `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`, `:yin.k/awaiting-grant`, `:yin.k/not-holder`, `:yin.k/unsatisfied` |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Amended 2026-10-16 (module-pins, R4).** After custody validation and\\\\\\\\nbefore attachment, every carried install child must have its manifest\\\\\\\\naddress listed under its module name in the receiving composition's\\\\\\\\n`opts {:yin.k/admitted {name manifest-address}}`. The default is empty:\\\\\\\\nan absent or different address refuses as\\\\\\\\n`{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied\\\\\\\\n  :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}`.\\\\\\\\nThis applies to children throughout the task tree, including fenced\\\\\\\\nrestoration; `holder.export/rehydrate-fenced` forwards the composition's\\\\\\\\n`:yin.k/admitted` option to the lower. Restore drops the sender's\\\\\\\\n`:yin.admit/id`, `:yin.admit/decision`,\\\\\\\\n`:yin.admit/asserters` and `:yin.admit/address` from each retained install\\\\\\\\nresponse before `link-install` can record them as receiver evidence. The\\\\\\\\ncomposition supplies admissions from its own policy, never from the pack.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThen **attachment** (step 11, `attach-streams!`): one `attach!` per\\\\\\\\ndistinct stream identity of the whole tree, `:yin.k/unsatisfied\\\\\\\\n{:dao.stream/identity …}` when the composition declines. Then **restore**\\\\\\\\n(step 12, `restore-task`): the carried vectors attached by A into a\\\\\\\\n  shape, image admission and blocked child, then requires a non-nil parent\\\\\\\\n  equal to response `:yin.link/id`. The manifest's semantic derivation\\\\\\\\n  address must hash the response's derivation record; its input equals\\\\\\\\n  the manifest tree and its output equals the image vector's A.\\\\\\\\n  This verifies response self-consistency. Amended 2026-10-16 (R4): the\\\\\\\\n  lower additionally requires the receiver composition's explicit\\\\\\\\n  `:yin.k/admitted {name manifest-address}` before attaching any stream,\\\\\\\\n  and drops the sender's admission evidence on restore.\\\\\\\\n- **Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)** — Reason: 7a implements the op-id grammar; correlation checks remain narrower.\\\\\\\\n  **6b Q4, CLOSED for operation ids; correlation agreement remains open.**\\\\\\\\n  `custody-baseline` checks retained put/FFI-request/link-request ids\\\\\\\\n  throughout the tree: exact sequences below next-op-seq, uniqueness,\\\\\\\\n  origin required, and no id naming the root's own occurrence. Fork trees\\\\\\\\n**Amended 2026-10-16 (R4).** Self-consistency does not admit a carried\\\\\\\\nchild into the receiver's installation family. Before any stream attach,\\\\\\\\nthe lower additionally requires the receiving composition's opts\\\\\\\\n`:yin.k/admitted {name manifest-address}` to list the child's manifest\\\\\\\\naddress under its name. Default empty refuses with\\\\\\\\n`{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied\\\\\\\\n  :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}`. Restore drops\\\\\\\\nthe sender's four `:yin.admit/*` decision fields from the retained\\\\\\\\nresponse before `link-install` can record them on the receiver's entry.\\\\\\\\nThis changes admission behavior, not the `:install` row's slots.\\\\\\\\nA remains the only code identity and the Universal AST is never lost.\\\\\\\\nNo new resolver or independent claimed-image-address check is added.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 5.5 The root\\\\\\\\n**Amended 2026-10-1