{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'PATH=/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin:$PATH /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/python3 -B -c '\"'import json,pathlib; names=[\\\"1794720000000-architect-confirm-round.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\\",\\\"1794820000000-architect-confirm3.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\\"]; [(print(\\\"LOG\\\",n),[(print(x[\\\"item\\\"].get(\\\"text\\\",\\\"\\\"))) for l in (pathlib.Path(\\\"collab/orch-lane\\\")/n).read_text().splitlines() if l.startswith(\\\"{\\\") for x in [json.loads(l)] if x.get(\\\"type\\\")==\\\"item.completed\\\" and x.get(\\\"item\\\",{}).get(\\\"type\\\")==\\\"agent_message\\\"]) for n in names]'\"","aggregated_output":"LOG 1794720000000-architect-confirm-round.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\nI’ll check the architecture rules and both commits, then give each unit a verdict. For P8, I’ll distinguish approval of the procedure from confirmation of the pending measured records.\nI’m using the code-review-pr skill for this confirmation pass, focused on the cited fixes and their acceptance boundaries.\nThe P1 diff removes the out-of-scope `fesc` reference and places the drain after the shutdown escape. The P8 manifest still has the three stale records, consistent with the remeasurement being pending. I’m checking the P9 edge cases and P1 fatal-bypass path before assigning verdicts.\nP9 still has contract defects despite the reported green gate: diff/intersect use loose equality, negative `strrpos` offsets remain wrong, and JSON encoding does not propagate nested failure correctly. The new tests also assert a nonexistent extraction constant. I’m checking the counterexamples against PHP 8.3 source so the required follow-up is concrete.\nFocused JVM probes reproduced the P9 failures: nested `json_encode([INF])` raises a host error, `json_decode(\"+1\")` returns `1`, and encoding ignores the supplied depth. For P1, the bundled closure check and linked-module manifest construction pass, and the shutdown-exit case returns `\"AS\"` with status `3`.\n**1. `d5f120d0` — CONFIRMED.**\n\nThe follow-up resolves both findings, including the linked-module boundary.\n\n- Bundled free-name checking returns no stray names; `module-spec` constructs successfully.\n- The shutdown-exit probe returns **`\"AS\"`, status `3`**.\n- Injecting `php/root-fatal` during the buffered shutdown callback returns **empty output and fatal `\"boom\"`**, bypassing the drain.\n\nThe seat may land this unit. [Corrected fallback and drain placement](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p1fix/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5189).\n\n**2. `0aa234e9` — DEFECT. Hold landing.**\n\nEmpty-search handling, nontruncating padding, single-array mapping keys, variadic mapping, null-binding existence, missing-name compact warnings, and the declaration-based resolution guard are repaired. Residual defects remain:\n\n- **P1 — Nested JSON encoding failure escapes into a host error.** `json_encode([INF])` reproduces `\"data primitive refused\"`: the array encoder concatenates its opening delimiter with the child’s `false` result. Without throw mode, PHP returns `false` without the newly introduced warning. [Encoder](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:648), [PHP 8.3 implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json.c).\n\n- **P2 — Negative `strrpos` offsets remain incorrect.** `strrpos(\"hello\", \"l\", -2)` reproduces **2**; PHP requires **3**. The new test pins the wrong answer. Offsets outside the haystack also need `ValueError`. [Implementation](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:52), [incorrect assertion](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/test/yang/php/antlr/builtin_surfaces_test.clj:37), [PHP source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/string.c).\n\n- **P2 — Array comparisons remain wrong.** Diff/intersect still use loose equality: `count(array_diff([\"1.0\"], [\"1\"]))` reproduces **0**, requiring **1** under [PHP’s string comparison](https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.array-diff.php). Unique’s flag dispatch is also misnumbered: `SORT_REGULAR` is **0**, numeric **1**, string **2**. The regular-mode counterexample reproduces two retained values instead of one. [Comparison code](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:503), [PHP flag definitions](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/php_array.h).\n\n- **P2 — Splice replacement conversion is incomplete.** Reusing `spread-loop` preserves replacement string keys, which PHP discards. Explicit `null` becomes one null element instead of an empty replacement array. [Splice implementation](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:431), [PHP contract](https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.array-splice.php).\n\n- **P2 — JSON grammar, depth, and options remain incomplete.** `json_decode(\"+1\")` reproduces integer **1**; raw control characters are also accepted. Encoding ignores argument 3: `json_encode([[1]], 0, 1)` succeeds. Decoding depth starts one level too low: `[1]` at depth 1 succeeds instead of failing. Other unsupported flags remain silently accepted. [Number parser](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:761), [depth/options](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:695), [PHP scanner](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json_scanner.re), [PHP depth initialization](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/json/json_parser.y).\n\n- **P2 — Extract/compact completion is overstated.** `EXTR_PREFIX_ONLY_IF_EXISTS` remains a nonexistent constant, now asserted by the tests. Invalid extraction modes, missing required prefixes, and invalid prefixes lack required validation. `EXTR_PREFIX_ALL` incorrectly rejects numeric keys: the focused probe imports **0** variables for `[0 => 5]` with prefix `\"p\"`; PHP imports `$p_0`. Empty prefixes also lose the mandatory underscore. `compact(1)` silently skips its required warning. [Constants](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/builtins.cljc:169), [extract/compact](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b1/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc:200), [PHP extraction and compact implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/array.c).\n\nThe reported **3/135/0** gate therefore does not establish contract completion. Correct the erroneous assertions and cover these counterexamples.\n\n**3. P8 manifest — CONFIRMED-WITH-EDITS, pending measured fold.**\n\n**The remeasure-and-fold procedure satisfies my ruling.** No additional semantic requirement is imposed.\n\nFor `bug44069`, `bug40809`, and `bug63055`:\n\n- Remove records that now pass.\n- For remaining failures, fold the measured result and update the classification/work item.\n- Retain the measured tree identity and run evidence; distinguish resource failures or timeouts from guest results.\n\nI independently checked **95 unique quick IDs**, matching descriptions and recorded total. The three stale slow records remain in the inspected artifact. The seat may land after folding the measurements and checking manifest consistency; this is conditional authority, not confirmation of results still pending.\n\nRead-only review completed with focused JVM probes and static/source checks. No files changed or suites rerun.\nLOG 1794820000000-architect-confirm3.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\nI’ll use the code-review-pr skill to check the origin tips, follow-up diffs, and recorded evidence, then issue a landing verdict for each branch.\nThe requested commits are available locally, but the local origin refs for P1 and P5 are older, and the remote lookup failed. I’ll verify the remote tips separately and check the exact commits meanwhile. P8 also has a later fold commit, `dbe9e072`, containing the timeout record described in your brief.\nThe live remote tips differ from the brief: P1 is at `0eade311` and P5 at `e39e1912`; neither includes its follow-up commit. P8 is at `dbe9e072`. I also found a P5 residual: the test drops the empty-buffer notice, but the recorded Verdict 2 explicitly required the engine to emit it and prohibited normalizing it away.\nP8’s manifest parses and has 95 unique quick IDs and 7 slow records. Two residuals prevent confirmation: `bug40809` still has `:feature :undefined-builtin`, and the claim that `str_replace` is absent conflicts with the reviewed tree, which registers and includes its implementation. The fold lacks a measured-tree hash and run-evidence reference to reconcile that conflict.\n1. **P1 — CONFIRMED for `d5f120d0`; origin-tip DEFECT.** The commit matches the previously confirmed escape/drain repair. **The seat may land `d5f120d0`.** However, live origin still points to `0eade311`, which lacks that repair. Advance origin before merging.\n\n2. **P5 — DEFECT.** Fixture repair, class-derived errno comparison, ordered request vectors, exit-status checking, and P5 banner are confirmed in `a7cf7a0f`. But `request_context_test.clj:36` removes the empty-`ob_end_clean` notice. Verdict 2 explicitly required emitting errno **8** in the engine and prohibited normalizing away this missing diagnostic. The reported **3/35/0** therefore does not close that finding. Also, live origin remains at `e39e1912`, without `a7cf7a0f`.\n\n3. **P8 — DEFECT at actual origin tip `dbe9e072`** (`514fae8d` plus timeout fold). Manifest parsing and **95 unique quick IDs / 7 slow records** check out. Residuals:\n   - `bug40809` still carries `:feature :undefined-builtin` despite its timeout result.\n   - This tree already registers `str_replace`, defines `php/bi-str-replace`, and includes those definitions in the prelude. The retained undefined-function observation needs reconciliation with that tree.\n   - The fold supplies no measured-tree hash or run-evidence reference establishing the claimed measurements. Retain those before confirmation; no replacement outcome should be inferred statically.\n\nRead-only review; no files changed or behavioral suites rerun. Only the exact P1 commit has renewed landing authority.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show a7cf7a0f:src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show a7cf7a0f:test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5.cljc; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show d5f120d0:src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '3060,3165p'; cat deps.edn | head -130; which bb clojure\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.php.oracle\n  \"PHP 8.3 CLI oracle runner for `yang.php.antlr.programs`\n   (docs/design/yang.php.md sections 14, 17.3).\n\n   For every fixture in `programs/fixtures` (plus `matrix-source` and\n   `float-cases`), writes the PHP source to a temporary file and runs:\n     docker run --rm -v <dir>:/w -w /w php:8.3-cli php \\\\\n       -d display_errors=1 -d html_errors=0 -d error_reporting=E_ALL \\\\\n       -d log_errors=0 <file>\n   Parses stdout into `:out`, `:diag` (`[[errno message] ...]`) and `:uncaught`\n   (`{:class c :message m}`), and compares against each fixture's expectation\n   (or `:departure/:zend` for departure fixtures).\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    [clojure.java.shell :as sh]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs :as programs]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p3b :as p3b]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p4 :as p4]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p5 :as p5]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p6 :as p6])\n  (:import\n    (java.nio.charset\n      StandardCharsets)\n    (java.nio.file\n      Files)\n    (java.nio.file.attribute\n      FileAttribute)))\n\n\n(def banner\n  \"The pinned PHP 8.3 CLI oracle provenance banner.\"\n  p3b/banner)\n\n\n(def p5-banner\n  \"The P5 request-context run's own provenance banner (version/host/date of\n  the P5 recording pass, not P3-b's).\"\n  \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\")\n\n\n(def ^:private errno-of\n  {\"Warning\" 2,\n   \"Notice\" 8,\n   \"Deprecated\" 8192,\n   \"Fatal error\" 1})\n\n\n(defn class-derived?\n  \"Whether the recorded diag entry carries a class-derived errno: the runner\n  parses only the `Warning|Notice|...` kind line, so the recorded number is\n  derived from the message class, not the true constant (e.g. `Notice` parses\n  to 8 where the engine's semantic truth for `E_USER_NOTICE` is 1024).\"\n  [diag-entry]\n  (boolean (:yang.php.oracle/class-derived (meta diag-entry))))\n\n\n(defn- mark-class-derived\n  \"Mark a recorded `[errno message]` pair as class-derived (see [[class-derived?]]).\"\n  [pair]\n  (with-meta pair {:yang.php.oracle/class-derived true}))\n\n\n(defn errno-match?\n  \"Whether expected errno `e` matches recorded diag entry `a`: identical\n  numbers match, and a 1024-vs-8 mismatch counts as equal ONLY when the oracle\n  record is marked class-derived.\"\n  [e a]\n  (let [[actual-errno] a]\n    (or (= e actual-errno)\n        (and (= 1024 e) (= 8 actual-errno) (class-derived? a)))))\n\n\n(defn diag-match?\n  \"Whether the expected diag vector matches the recorded one entry-wise under\n  [[errno-match?]] (messages compare literally).\"\n  [expected-diag actual-diag]\n  (and (= (count expected-diag) (count actual-diag))\n       (every? true? (map (fn [[e-errno e-msg] a]\n                            (and (errno-match? e-errno a)\n                                 (= e-msg (second a))))\n                          expected-diag actual-diag))))\n\n\n(defn- location-pattern\n  \"The regex source of a PHP source location below `/w/`: the entry `file`\n   itself, or, for a multi-unit fixture run in `/w/<unit-dir>`, any unit file\n   below the directory.\"\n  [file unit-dir]\n  (if unit-dir\n    (str (java.util.regex.Pattern/quote unit-dir) \"/[^\\\\s:]+\")\n    (java.util.regex.Pattern/quote file)))\n\n\n(defn- strip-location\n  ([s file] (strip-location s file nil))\n  ([s file unit-dir]\n   (str/replace s\n                (re-pattern (str \" in /w/\" (location-pattern file unit-dir) \" on line \\\\d+\"))\n                \"\")))\n\n\n(defn parse-stdout\n  \"Parse PHP CLI stdout for `/w/<file>` into\n   `{:out <string> :diag [[errno msg] ...] :uncaught {:class c :message m}-or-nil}`.\n   With `unit-dir`, locations in any file below `/w/<unit-dir>` are stripped\n   (a multi-unit fixture).\"\n  ([raw file] (parse-stdout raw file nil))\n  ([raw file unit-dir]\n   (let [qfile (location-pattern file unit-dir)\n         strip-location (fn [s file] (strip-location s file unit-dir))\n         ;; The uncaught block ends at PHP's own terminator, so output written\n         ;; after it (shutdown functions, destructors) stays in :out.\n         uncaught-re (re-pattern\n                       (str \"(?s)\\\\nFatal error: Uncaught ([^:]+): ([^\\\\r\\\\n]*) in /w/\"\n                            qfile\n                            \":\\\\d+\\\\nStack trace:\\\\n.*?\\\\n  thrown in /w/\"\n                            qfile\n                            \" on line \\\\d+\\\\n\"))\n         fatal-re (re-pattern\n                    (str \"\\\\nFatal error: ([^\\\\r\\\\n]*) in /w/\"\n                         qfile\n                         \" on line \\\\d+\\\\n\"))\n         diag-re (re-pattern\n                   (str \"\\\\n(Warning|Notice|Deprecated): ([^\\\\r\\\\n]*?) in /w/\"\n                        qfile\n                        \" on line \\\\d+\\\\n\"))\n         [without-fatal uncaught]\n         (if-let [[_ cls msg] (re-find uncaught-re raw)]\n           [(str/replace raw uncaught-re \"\")\n            {:class cls, :message (strip-location msg file)}]\n           (if-let [[_ msg] (re-find fatal-re raw)]\n             [(str/replace raw fatal-re \"\")\n              {:class \"Error\", :message (strip-location msg file)}]\n             [raw nil]))\n         diags (volatile! [])\n         out (str/replace without-fatal\n                          diag-re\n                          (fn [[_ kind msg]]\n                            (vswap! diags conj (mark-class-derived [(get errno-of kind) (strip-location msg file)]))\n                            \"\"))]\n     {:out out,\n      :diag @diags,\n      :uncaught uncaught})))\n\n\n(defn run-php-file\n  \"Run `<file>` inside `<dir>` via Docker `php:8.3-cli` and return the parsed\n   `{:out :diag :uncaught :exit}`. With `unit-dir`, the working directory is\n   `/w/<unit-dir>` and `file` is relative to it (a multi-unit fixture).\"\n  ([dir file] (run-php-file dir file nil))\n  ([dir file unit-dir]\n   (let [{:keys [out err exit]}\n         (sh/sh \"docker\" \"run\" \"--rm\"\n                \"-v\" (str (.toAbsolutePath (.toPath (io/file dir))) \":/w\")\n                \"-w\" (if unit-dir (str \"/w/\" unit-dir) \"/w\")\n                \"php:8.3-cli\" \"php\"\n                \"-d\" \"display_errors=1\"\n                \"-d\" \"html_errors=0\"\n                \"-d\" \"error_reporting=E_ALL\"\n                \"-d\" \"log_errors=0\"\n                file\n                :out-enc \"UTF-8\")]\n     (assoc (parse-stdout out (if unit-dir (str unit-dir \"/\" file) file) unit-dir)\n            :err err\n            :exit exit))))\n\n\n(defn- write-source!\n  [dir file ^String source]\n  (Files/write (.toPath (io/file dir file))\n               (.getBytes source StandardCharsets/UTF_8)\n               (make-array java.nio.file.OpenOption 0)))\n\n\n(defn- unit-actual\n  \"Run the multi-unit `fixture`: every unit is written below `<dir>/<id>/`,\n   `main.php` is run with that directory as the working directory, and\n   `/w/<id>` is replaced by `.` in everything the program printed (the\n   comparison's definition, plan P6 2.5 rule 2; corner C37).\"\n  [dir {:keys [id units main], :or {main \"main.php\"}}]\n  (let [unit-dir (name id)\n        norm (fn [s] (str/replace s (str \"/w/\" unit-dir) \".\"))]\n    (doseq [[path source] units]\n      (let [f (io/file dir unit-dir path)]\n        (io/make-parents f)\n        (write-source! dir (str unit-dir \"/\" path) source)))\n    (let [actual (run-php-file dir main unit-dir)]\n      (-> actual\n          (update :out norm)\n          (update :diag (fn [ds] (mapv (fn [[errno msg]] [errno (norm msg)]) ds)))\n          (update :uncaught #(some-> % (update :message norm)))))))\n\n\n(defn check-fixture\n  \"Run `fixture` in temporary directory `dir` and return a check record.\"\n  [dir {:keys [id source units out diag uncaught departure gap oracle], :as fixture}]\n  (let [file (str (name id) \".php\")]\n    (when-not units (write-source! dir file source))\n    (let [actual (if units (unit-actual dir fixture) (run-php-file dir file))\n          expected-out (cond departure (:zend departure)\n                             gap \"\"\n                             :else out)\n          expected-diag (vec (cond departure (:zend-diag departure)\n                                   gap []\n                                   :else (or diag [])))\n          expected-uncaught (cond departure (:zend-uncaught departure)\n                                  gap nil\n                                  :else uncaught)\n          pass? (and (not= :pending oracle)\n                     (= expected-out (:out actual))\n                     (= expected-diag (:diag actual))\n                     (= expected-uncaught (:uncaught actual)))]\n      {:id id,\n       :pass? pass?,\n       :oracle oracle,\n       :gap gap,\n       :departure departure,\n       :expected {:out expected-out, :diag expected-diag, :uncaught expected-uncaught},\n       :actual (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught])})))\n\n\n(defn- check-matrix\n  [dir]\n  (let [file \"scalar-comparison-matrix.php\"\n        _ (write-source! dir file programs/matrix-source)\n        actual (run-php-file dir file)\n        [eq sp] (str/split-lines (:out actual))\n        w (count programs/matrix-values)\n        actual-eq (mapv #(apply str %) (partition w eq))\n        actual-sp (mapv #(apply str (map {\\0 \"<\", \\1 \"=\", \\2 \">\"} %)) (partition w sp))]\n    {:id :scalar-comparison-matrix,\n     :pass? (and (= programs/equal-matrix actual-eq)\n                 (= programs/spaceship-matrix actual-sp)\n                 (empty? (:diag actual))\n                 (nil? (:uncaught actual))),\n     :expected {:eq programs/equal-matrix, :sp programs/spaceship-matrix},\n     :actual {:eq actual-eq, :sp actual-sp, :diag (:diag actual), :uncaught (:uncaught actual)}}))\n\n\n(defn- check-floats\n  [dir]\n  (let [file \"float-cases.php\"\n        src (str \"<?php\\n\"\n                 (apply str (for [[lit] programs/float-cases]\n                              (str \"echo \" lit \", \\\"|\\\"; var_dump(\" lit \");\\n\"))))\n        expected (apply str (for [[_ echo dump] programs/float-cases]\n                              (str echo \"|float(\" dump \")\\n\")))\n        _ (write-source! dir file src)\n        actual (run-php-file dir file)]\n    {:id :float-cases,\n     :pass? (and (= expected (:out actual))\n                 (empty? (:diag actual))\n                 (nil? (:uncaught actual))),\n     :expected {:out expected, :diag [], :uncaught nil},\n     :actual (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught])}))\n\n\n(defn- php-literal\n  \"The PHP literal of request-record scalar `v`: strings single-quoted\n   (escaping backslash and quote, the only two escapes there), ints bare.\n   Key coercion (numeric strings to ints) is left to PHP itself, exactly as\n   the engine's `php/array-key` performs it.\"\n  [v]\n  (cond (string? v) (str \"'\" (str/replace v #\"\\\\|'\" (fn [[c]] (str \"\\\\\" c))) \"'\")\n        (integer? v) (str v)\n        :else (throw (ex-info \"p5 oracle: non-scalar in request record\" {:value v}))))\n\n(defn- request-pairs\n  \"Ordered `[k v]` pairs of request-array `arr`: the engine's ordered entry\n   vectors are accepted as-is; otherwise pairs follow the array's `:order`\n   (the engine's insertion order).\"\n  [arr]\n  (when arr\n    (if (sequential? arr)\n      (mapv vec arr)\n      (mapv (fn [k] [k (get (:index arr) k)]) (:order arr)))))\n\n(defn- php-array-literal\n  \"The PHP `array(...)` literal of request-array `arr`.\"\n  [arr]\n  (if (empty? (request-pairs arr))\n    \"array()\"\n    (str \"array(\"\n         (str/join \", \" (map (fn [[k v]]\n                               (str (php-literal k) \" => \" (php-literal v)))\n                             (request-pairs arr)))\n         \")\")))\n\n(defn p5-prologue\n  \"The `auto_prepend_file` prologue assigning the superglobals from the\n   fixture `:request` record, mirroring `php/bind-request!` (prelude\n   section `request and output`): `$_GET` is the query, `$_POST` the body,\n   `$_COOKIE` the cookies, `$_SERVER` the server fields with\n   `REQUEST_METHOD`/`REQUEST_URI` appended, `$_ENV` the env, `$_FILES` the\n   files, and `$_REQUEST` is `array_merge($_GET, $_POST)` (POST wins, the\n   engine's `php/merge-loop` over `[get post]`).\"\n  [request]\n  (let [method (or (:php.request/method request) \"\")\n        uri (or (:php.request/uri request) \"\")]\n    (str \"<?php\\n\"\n         \"$_GET = \" (php-array-literal (:php.request/query request)) \";\\n\"\n         \"$_POST = \" (php-array-literal (:php.request/body request)) \";\\n\"\n         \"$_COOKIE = \" (php-array-literal (:php.request/cookies request)) \";\\n\"\n         \"$_SERVER = \" (php-array-literal (:php.request/server request)) \";\\n\"\n         \"$_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] = \" (php-literal method) \";\\n\"\n         \"$_SERVER['REQUEST_URI'] = \" (php-literal uri) \";\\n\"\n         \"$_ENV = \" (php-array-literal (:php.request/env request)) \";\\n\"\n         \"$_FILES = \" (php-array-literal (:php.request/files request)) \";\\n\"\n         \"$_REQUEST = array_merge($_GET, $_POST);\\n\")))\n\n(defn run-php-file-with-prepend\n  \"Run `<file>` inside `<dir>` via Docker `php:8.3-cli` with `prepend-file`\n   (a path relative to `<dir>`) as `auto_prepend_file`, and return the\n   parsed `{:out :diag :uncaught :exit}`.\"\n  [dir file prepend-file]\n  (let [{:keys [out err exit]}\n        (sh/sh \"docker\" \"run\" \"--rm\"\n               \"-v\" (str (.toAbsolutePath (.toPath (io/file dir))) \":/w\")\n               \"-w\" \"/w\"\n               \"php:8.3-cli\" \"php\"\n               \"-d\" \"display_errors=1\"\n               \"-d\" \"html_errors=0\"\n               \"-d\" \"error_reporting=E_ALL\"\n               \"-d\" \"log_errors=0\"\n               \"-d\" (str \"auto_prepend_file=/w/\" prepend-file)\n               file\n               :out-enc \"UTF-8\")]\n    (assoc (parse-stdout out file nil)\n           :err err\n           :exit exit)))\n\n(defn check-p5-fixture\n  \"Run P5 `fixture` in temporary directory `dir`: the fixture source plus,\n   for `:request`-bearing fixtures, the [[p5-prologue]] as\n   `auto_prepend_file`. Returns a check record like [[check-fixture]].\"\n  [dir {:keys [id source request out diag uncaught status oracle]}]\n  (let [file (str (name id) \".php\")\n        pre (str (name id) \"-pre.php\")]\n    (write-source! dir file source)\n    (when request (write-source! dir pre (p5-prologue request)))\n    (let [actual (if request\n                   (run-php-file-with-prepend dir file pre)\n                   (run-php-file dir file))\n          expected-out (or out \"\")\n          expected-diag (vec (or diag []))\n          pass? (and (not= :pending oracle)\n                     (= expected-out (:out actual))\n                     (diag-match? expected-diag (:diag actual))\n                     (= uncaught (:uncaught actual))\n                     (or (nil? status) (= status (:exit actual))))]\n      {:id id,\n       :pass? pass?,\n       :oracle oracle,\n       :expected {:out expected-out, :diag expected-diag, :uncaught uncaught, :status status},\n       :actual (assoc (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught]) :exit (:exit actual))})))\n\n(defn run-p5\n  \"Run all `p5/fixtures` (the request-context fixtures) against\n   `php:8.3-cli`.\"\n  []\n  (let [dir (.toFile (Files/createTempDirectory \"yang-php-oracle-p5-\"\n                                                (make-array FileAttribute 0)))]\n    (try\n      (mapv #(check-p5-fixture dir %) p5/fixtures)\n      (finally\n        (doseq [f (reverse (file-seq dir))]\n          (.delete ^java.io.File f))))))\n\n(defn print-fold\n  \"Print the fold lines for `results`: one paste-ready record per fixture\n   in the P4 [[p4/pin]] shape `{:oracle p5-banner :out :diag :uncaught}`.\"\n  [results]\n  (doseq [{:keys [id actual]} results]\n    (println \"FOLD\" (name id)\n             (pr-str (assoc (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught])\n                            :oracle p5-banner)))))\n\n(defn run-all\n  \"Run all `programs/fixtures`, `matrix-source` and `float-cases` against\n   `php:8.3-cli`.\"\n  []\n  (let [dir (.toFile (Files/createTempDirectory \"yang-php-oracle-\"\n                                                (make-array FileAttribute 0)))]\n    (try\n      (-> (mapv #(check-fixture dir %) (concat programs/fixtures p3b/all-fixtures p4/all-fixtures p6/all-fixtures))\n          (conj (check-matrix dir))\n          (conj (check-floats dir)))\n      (finally\n        (doseq [f (reverse (file-seq dir))]\n          (.delete ^java.io.File f))))))\n\n\n(defn -main\n  [& args]\n  (when (some #{\"--print-prologue\"} args)\n    (let [id (keyword (or (second (drop-while #(not= \"--print-prologue\" %) args))\n                          \"superglobals-from-request\"))\n          fixture (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) p5/fixtures))]\n      (when-not fixture\n        (println \"Unknown P5 fixture:\" id)\n        (System/exit 2))\n      ;; Dry run: no docker, no oracle. Print the generated prologue for\n      ;; eyeball comparison against the engine's expected superglobal\n      ;; values (the fixture's hand-derived :out is the reference).\n      (print (p5-prologue (:request fixture)))\n      (flush)\n      (shutdown-agents)\n      (System/exit 0)))\n  (when (some #{\"--p5\"} args)\n    (let [results (run-p5)\n          recorded (filter #(= :pending (:oracle %)) results)\n          failures (remove #(or (:pass? %) (= :pending (:oracle %))) results)]\n      (println \"Banner:\" p5-banner)\n      (println \"Checked:\" (count results) \"P5 targets; failures:\" (count failures))\n      (print-fold recorded)\n      (doseq [f failures]\n        (println \"FAIL\" (:id f))\n        (println \"  expected:\" (pr-str (:expected f)))\n        (println \"  actual:  \" (pr-str (:actual f))))\n      (shutdown-agents)\n      (when (seq failures)\n        (System/exit 1))\n      (System/exit 0)))\n  (let [results (run-all)\n        recorded (filter #(= :pending (:oracle %)) results)\n        failures (remove #(or (:pass? %) (= :pending (:oracle %))) results)]\n    (println \"Banner:\" banner)\n    (println \"Checked:\" (count results) \"targets; failures:\" (count failures))\n    (doseq [f recorded]\n      (println \"RECORD\" (:id f) (pr-str (:actual f)) \"matches-pinned-out:\" (boolean (:pass? f))))\n    (doseq [f failures]\n      (println \"FAIL\" (:id f))\n      (println \"  expected:\" (pr-str (:expected f)))\n      (println \"  actual:  \" (pr-str (:actual f))))\n    (shutdown-agents)\n    (when (seq failures)\n      (System/exit 1))))\n(ns yang.php.antlr.programs-p5\n  \"P5 request-context fixtures. Expectations are hand-derived from PHP 8.3;\n  every fixture remains available to the oracle recording pass.\")\n\n\n(defn request-array\n  [entries]\n  {:php/type :array, :index (into {} entries), :order (mapv first entries)})\n\n\n(def request\n  {:php.request/method \"POST\"\n   :php.request/uri \"/hello?a=1\"\n   :php.request/query (request-array [[\"a\" \"1\"] [\"shared\" \"get\"]])\n   :php.request/headers (request-array [[\"X-Test\" \"yes\"]])\n   :php.request/cookies (request-array [[\"session\" \"abc\"]])\n   :php.request/body (request-array [[\"b\" \"2\"] [\"shared\" \"post\"]])\n   :php.request/server (request-array [[\"SERVER_NAME\" \"fixture.test\"]])\n   :php.request/env (request-array [[\"APP_ENV\" \"test\"]])\n   :php.request/files (request-array [[\"upload\" \"fixture\"]])})\n\n\n(defn- fx\n  [id source out & {:as more}]\n  (merge {:id id, :group :request-context, :source source, :out out,\n          :request request, :oracle :pending}\n         more))\n\n\n(def fixtures\n  [(fx :superglobals-from-request\n       (str \"<?php echo $_GET['a'], $_POST['b'], $_COOKIE['session'],\"\n            \" $_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'], $_SERVER['REQUEST_URI'],\"\n            \" $_SERVER['SERVER_NAME'], $_ENV['APP_ENV'], $_FILES['upload'],\"\n            \" $_REQUEST['a'], $_REQUEST['b'], $_REQUEST['shared'];\")\n       \"12abcPOST/hello?a=1fixture.testtestfixture12post\" :diag [] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\")\n   (fx :output-buffering\n       \"<?php ob_start(); echo 'a'; echo ob_get_contents(); ob_start(); echo 'b'; echo ob_get_clean(); echo ob_get_clean(); echo 'c';\"\n       \"aabc\" :diag [] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\")\n   (fx :output-buffer-flush\n       \"<?php ob_start(); echo 'a'; ob_end_flush(); echo 'b'; var_dump(ob_end_clean());\"\n       \"abbool(false)\\n\" :diag [[8 \"ob_end_clean(): Failed to delete buffer. No buffer to delete\"]] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\")\n   (fx :headers-cookies-status\n       \"<?php header('X-One: 1'); setcookie('sid', 'abc'); http_response_code(201); echo http_response_code();\"\n       \"201\" :diag [] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\"\n       :response [{:php.response/header \"X-One: 1\", :replace true}\n                  {:php.response/cookie {:name \"sid\", :value \"abc\"}}\n                  {:php.response/status 201}\n                  {:php.response/body \"201\"}])\n   (fx :headers-after-output\n       \"<?php echo 'x'; header('X-Late: 1'); var_dump(headers_sent());\"\n       \"xbool(true)\\n\" :diag [[2 \"Cannot modify header information - headers already sent by (output started at /w/headers-after-output.php:1)\"]] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\"\n       :response [{:php.response/body \"xbool(true)\\n\"}])\n   (fx :error-handler-and-warnings\n       (str \"<?php set_error_handler(function($n, $s) { echo 'H', $n, ':', $s; });\"\n            \" trigger_error('first', E_USER_WARNING); restore_error_handler();\"\n            \" trigger_error('second', E_USER_NOTICE);\")\n       \"H512:first\" :diag [[1024 \"second\"]] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\")\n   (fx :exit-runs-shutdown\n       \"<?php register_shutdown_function(function() { echo 'S'; }); echo 'A'; exit(7); echo 'B';\"\n       \"AS\" :diag [] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\"\n       :status 7)\n   (fx :exit-string\n       \"<?php echo 'A'; die('B'); echo 'C';\"\n       \"AB\" :diag [] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\"\n       :status 0)])\n    [php/inherit-interface\n     (fn [st i]\n       (assoc st\n              :consts (php/vfold (fn [acc e] (php/vput acc :name e)) (get st :consts) (get i :constants) 0)\n              :methods (php/vfold (fn [acc m]\n                                    (if (nil? (php/vfind acc :lc (get m :lc) 0)) (php/vconj acc m) acc))\n                                  (get st :methods) (get i :methods) 0)))]\n    [php/inherit-state\n     (fn [parent ifaces]\n       (php/vfold php/inherit-interface\n                  (if (nil? parent)\n                    (assoc {} :consts [] :props [] :statics [] :methods [])\n                    (assoc {} :consts (php/or-default (get parent :constants) [])\n                           :props (php/or-default (get parent :props-decl) [])\n                           :statics (php/or-default (get parent :static-props) [])\n                           :methods (php/or-default (get parent :methods) [])))\n                  ifaces 0))]\n    ;; ---- traits: copied into the class, methods specialized to the using class\n    [php/rule-excludes?\n     ;; an insteadof rule that drops `tlc::mlc`\n     (fn [rules tlc mlc]\n       (php/vfold\n         (fn [hit r]\n           (if hit\n             true\n             (if (= (php/lc (get r :method)) mlc)\n               (php/vfold (fn [h x] (if h true (= (php/lc x) tlc))) false (get r :excluded) 0)\n               false)))\n         false rules 0))]\n    [php/rule-vis\n     ;; the visibility an `as` rule without alias gives `tlc::mlc`, or nil\n     (fn [rules tlc mlc]\n       (php/vfold\n         (fn [v r]\n           (if (nil? v)\n             (if (nil? (get r :alias))\n               (if (= (php/lc (get r :method)) mlc)\n                 (if (if (nil? (get r :trait)) true (= (php/lc (get r :trait)) tlc)) (get r :vis) nil)\n                 nil)\n               nil)\n             v))\n         nil rules 0))]\n    [php/trait-method-add\n     ;; add trait method `tm` (from trait `t`) to the staged vector `tm-list`\n     (fn [tm-list cls t tm name]\n       (let [m (assoc (php/make-method cls tm) :from-trait (get t :name) :name name :lc (php/lc name))\n             prior (php/vfind tm-list :lc (get m :lc) 0)]\n         (if (nil? prior)\n           (php/vconj tm-list m)\n           (if (= (get prior :abstract?) true)\n             (php/vput tm-list :lc m)\n             (if (= (get m :abstract?) true)\n               tm-list\n               (php/throw-error\n                 \"Error\"\n                 (data/str-concat \"Trait method \" (get t :name) \"::\" (get tm :name)\n                                  \" has not been applied as \" cls \"::\" (get tm :name)\n                                  \", because of collision with \" (get prior :from-trait) \"::\"\n                                  (get prior :name))))))))]\n    [php/apply-trait\n     (fn [cls rules]\n       (fn [tm-list t]\n         (php/vfold\n           (fn [acc tm]\n             (let [tlc (php/lc (get t :name))\n                   mlc (get tm :lc)\n                   dropped (php/rule-excludes? (php/or-default (get rules :insteadof) []) tlc mlc)\n                   acc1 (if dropped\n                          acc\n                          (let [vis (php/rule-vis (php/or-default (get rules :as) []) tlc mlc)\n                                tm2 (if (nil? vis) tm (assoc tm :vis vis))]\n                            (php/trait-method-add acc cls t tm2 (get tm :name))))]\n               (php/vfold\n                 (fn [a r]\n                   (if (if (nil? (get r :alias)) false (= (php/lc (get r :method)) mlc))\n                     (if (if (nil? (get r :trait)) true (= (php/lc (get r :trait)) tlc))\n                       (php/trait-method-add a cls t\n                                             (if (nil? (get r :vis)) tm (assoc tm :vis (get r :vis)))\n                                             (get r :alias))\n                       a)\n                     a))\n                 acc1 (php/or-default (get rules :as) []) 0)))\n           tm-list (get t :methods) 0)))]\n    [php/apply-traits\n     (fn [st cls traits rules]\n       (let [tms (php/vfold (php/apply-trait cls rules) [] traits 0)\n             consts (php/vfold\n                      (fn [acc t]\n                        (php/vfold (fn [a e] (php/vput a :name e)) acc (get t :constants) 0))\n                      (get st :consts) traits 0)\n             props (php/vfold\n                     (fn [acc t]\n                       (php/vfold (fn [a p] (php/vput a :id (php/make-prop cls p)))\n                                  acc (get t :props-decl) 0))\n                     (get st :props) traits 0)\n             statics (php/vfold\n                       (fn [acc t]\n                         (php/vfold (fn [a s] (php/vput a :name (php/make-static cls s)))\n                                    acc (get t :static-props) 0))\n                       (get st :statics) traits 0)]\n         (assoc st :consts consts :props props :statics statics\n                :methods (php/vfold php/put-method (get st :methods) tms 0))))]\n    [php/apply-own\n     (fn [st cls spec kind]\n       (let [consts (php/vfold (fn [acc s] (php/vput acc :name (php/make-const cls s)))\n                               (get st :consts) (php/or-default (get spec :consts) []) 0)\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\" \"build/antlr/php/classes\"\n         \"build/antlr/typescript/classes\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}\n                               ;; latte-kernel: the LaTTe proof assistant's kernel,\n                               ;; the differential oracle for the yang.clojure gap\n                               ;; program (pinned; MIT; dependency-free)\n                               latte-kernel/latte-kernel\n                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\"\n                                :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}\n                  ;; The guest recursion limit allows depth that needs more than the\n                  ;; JVM's platform default thread stack (1024 KB on Linux, 2048 KB on\n                  ;; macOS): under 1 MB the guard loses to a JVM StackOverflowError\n                  ;; before it can raise Python's RecursionError, so the same tests\n                  ;; pass on macOS and fail on Linux. 4 MB is twice the measured\n                  ;; macOS-default minimum, leaving headroom as the prelude grows.\n                  ;; Evidence: docs/agents/known-gaps.md (the recursion rows).\n                  ;; merged stack policy: -Xss64m supersedes the earlier -Xss4m —\n                  ;; deep assertion payloads (the PHPT selection diagnostics and\n                  ;; the conformance compositions) overflow smaller stacks in\n                  ;; clojure.test's printer on shiva (verified green at -Xss64m;\n                  ;; the 4m minimum for the prelude recursion rows still holds)\n                  :jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\" \"bu